# --- Never commit HP or Adobe content -------------------------------------
# ClickGraft ships no third-party application code. These patterns are a
# backstop: extracting an asar or copying a bundle into the working tree is a
# normal thing to do while debugging, and none of it may ever be published.
*.app/
*.asar
*.asar.unpacked/
hpclick-src/
backup*/
electron-v*-darwin-*.zip
SHASUMS256*.txt

# Build output
build/
build_*/
staging*/
dist/

# --- Python ----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# --- macOS -----------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

# --- Local scratch ---------------------------------------------------------
scratch/
*.log

# --- Local tooling config --------------------------------------------------
.claude/settings.local.json

# Deploy target — host/CT id are private network details.
site/deploy/deploy.env

# --- Code-review notes -----------------------------------------------------
# Output from review tools run against this tree. Working notes about the
# code's weaknesses, written for one person, in a repository anyone can read:
# a half-finished list of suspected flaws reads very differently to a stranger
# than to the person triaging it. Keep them local.
ag-review*.md
*-review.md
